- .env.example (modify)

## What to do
Copy lib/rate-limit.ts from origin/feat/otp-endpoints (commit 83e8702) to the eco-259-fix-tester-feedback-from-v01 branch. The file contains:

1. hashIdentifier() - HMAC-SHA256 hashing of identifiers (email/IP) to avoid PII in rate_limits table
2. checkRateLimit(identifier, endpoint, config) - Sliding window rate limit check via Supabase
3. recordRateLimitAttempt(identifier, endpoint) - Records an attempt
4. getClientIp(headers) - Extracts client IP from x-forwarded-for, x-real-ip, x-vercel-forwarded-for
5. RATE_LIMITS - Pre-configured rate limit settings object

The exact source to copy from: `git show origin/feat/otp-endpoints:lib/rate-limit.ts`

Adapt the RATE_LIMITS config to remove OTP-specific entries and add onboarding-relevant ones:

```ts
export const RATE_LIMITS = {
  passwordResetRequest: {
    byIp: { windowMs: 60 * 60 * 1000, maxAttempts: 10 },
    byEmail: { windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, maxAttempts: 3 },
  },
  passwordReset: {
    byIp: { windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, maxAttempts: 10 },
  },
  sendInviteEmail: {
    byIp: { windowMs: 60 * 60 * 1000, maxAttempts: 10 },
    byEmail: { windowMs: 5 * 60 * 1000, maxAttempts: 1 },
  },
  verifyInviteCode: {
    byIp: { windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, maxAttempts: 20 },
  },
  onboard: {
    byIp: { windowMs: 60 * 60 * 1000, maxAttempts: 5 },
  },
} as const;
```

Also add RATE_LIMIT_HMAC_KEY to .env.example with a comment.

## Don't
- Keep otpRequest/otpVerify entries in RATE_LIMITS (those are OTP-specific)
- Change the core checkRateLimit/recordRateLimitAttempt/getClientIp/hashIdentifier logic
- Import from any OTP-specific modules

## Files
- app/onboarding/api/send-invite-email/route.ts (modify)

## What to do
The send-invite-email route currently has inline ad-hoc rate limiting that:
- Stores raw email as identifier (PII leak in DB)
- Uses manual Supabase queries for rate checking
- Deletes old rate limit records instead of using sliding window

Refactor to use the shared rate limiter from lib/rate-limit.ts.

Replace the inline rate limiting block (lines ~72-100 approximately) with:

```ts
import { checkRateLimit, recordRateLimitAttempt, getClientIp, RATE_LIMITS } from '@/lib/rate-limit';

// Inside POST handler, after validation:
const clientIp = getClientIp(req.headers);

// Check IP rate limit
const ipLimit = await checkRateLimit(
  `ip:${clientIp}`,
  'send-invite-email',
  RATE_LIMITS.sendInviteEmail.byIp
);
if (!ipLimit.allowed) {
  return Response.json(
    { error: 'RateLimitExceeded', message: 'Too many requests', retryAfter: ipLimit.resetAt.toISOString() },
    { status: 429, headers: { 'Retry-After': String(Math.ceil((ipLimit.resetAt.getTime() - Date.now()) / 1000)) } }
  );
}

// Check email rate limit
const emailLimit = await checkRateLimit(
  `email:${email}`,
  'send-invite-email',
  RATE_LIMITS.sendInviteEmail.byEmail
);
if (!emailLimit.allowed) {
  return Response.json(
    { error: 'RateLimitExceeded', message: 'Please wait before requesting another invite code', retryAfter: emailLimit.resetAt.toISOString() },
    { status: 429, headers: { 'Retry-After': String(Math.ceil((emailLimit.resetAt.getTime() - Date.now()) / 1000)) } }
  );
}

// ... existing invite code + email send logic ...

// After successful email send, record attempts:
await recordRateLimitAttempt(`ip:${clientIp}`, 'send-invite-email');
await recordRateLimitAttempt(`email:${email}`, 'send-invite-email');
```

Remove the old inline rate limiting code (the manual supabase.from('rate_limits').select/delete/insert block).

## Don't
- Change the invite code generation or email sending logic
- Change the Zod schema validation
- Remove the Supabase null check (keep it for invite code logic)
- Add rate limiting to the catch block

## Files
- app/api/atproto/request-password-reset/route.ts (modify)

## What to do
Add IP-based and email-based rate limiting to the password reset request endpoint. This endpoint currently has zero rate limiting, making it vulnerable to abuse (email bombing, enumeration).

At the top of the POST handler, after the email validation block, add:

```ts
import { checkRateLimit, recordRateLimitAttempt, getClientIp, RATE_LIMITS } from '@/lib/rate-limit';

// Inside POST, after email validation passes:
const clientIp = getClientIp(req.headers);

const ipLimit = await checkRateLimit(
  `ip:${clientIp}`,
  'password-reset-request',
  RATE_LIMITS.passwordResetRequest.byIp
);
if (!ipLimit.allowed) {
  return new Response(
    JSON.stringify({ error: 'RateLimitExceeded', message: 'Too many requests' }),
    { status: 429, headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'Retry-After': String(Math.ceil((ipLimit.resetAt.getTime() - Date.now()) / 1000)) } }
  );
}

const emailLimit = await checkRateLimit(
  `email:${email}`,
  'password-reset-request',
  RATE_LIMITS.passwordResetRequest.byEmail
);
if (!emailLimit.allowed) {
  // Return generic success to prevent email enumeration
  return new Response(JSON.stringify({ success: true }), {
    status: 200,
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  });
}
```

After the PDS call succeeds (before the success return), record attempts:
```ts
await recordRateLimitAttempt(`ip:${clientIp}`, 'password-reset-request');
await recordRateLimitAttempt(`email:${email}`, 'password-reset-request');
```

IMPORTANT: When email rate limit is exceeded, return 200 success (not 429) to prevent email enumeration. Only IP rate limit returns 429.

## Don't
- Change the PDS proxy logic
- Change the email validation logic
- Add rate limiting to the catch block
- Return 429 for email-based rate limit (use 200 to prevent enumeration)

## Files
- app/api/atproto/reset-password/route.ts (modify)

## What to do
Add IP-based rate limiting to the password reset (token consumption) endpoint. This endpoint accepts a token + new password and currently has no rate limiting, allowing brute-force token guessing.

At the top of the POST handler, before body parsing, add:

```ts
import { checkRateLimit, recordRateLimitAttempt, getClientIp, RATE_LIMITS } from '@/lib/rate-limit';

// Inside POST, at the very start:
const clientIp = getClientIp(req.headers);

const ipLimit = await checkRateLimit(
  `ip:${clientIp}`,
  'password-reset',
  RATE_LIMITS.passwordReset.byIp
);
if (!ipLimit.allowed) {
  return new Response(
    JSON.stringify({ error: 'RateLimitExceeded', message: 'Too many requests' }),
    { status: 429, headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'Retry-After': String(Math.ceil((ipLimit.resetAt.getTime() - Date.now()) / 1000)) } }
  );
}
```

After the PDS call (regardless of success/failure), record the attempt:
```ts
await recordRateLimitAttempt(`ip:${clientIp}`, 'password-reset');
```

Note: Record attempt even on PDS failure to prevent brute-force token guessing.

## Don't
- Change the PDS proxy logic
- Change the token/password validation
- Add email-based rate limiting (tokens are not tied to emails in this endpoint)

