## What to do
Add IP-based rate limiting to the combined onboard endpoint. This endpoint creates accounts and initializes organizations. Without rate limiting, an attacker could mass-create accounts.

At the top of the POST handler, before formData parsing, add:

```ts
import { checkRateLimit, recordRateLimitAttempt, getClientIp, RATE_LIMITS } from '@/lib/rate-limit';

// Inside POST, at the very start:
const clientIp = getClientIp(req.headers);

const ipLimit = await checkRateLimit(
  `ip:${clientIp}`,
  'onboard',
  RATE_LIMITS.onboard.byIp
);
if (!ipLimit.allowed) {
  return Response.json(
    { error: 'RateLimitExceeded', message: 'Too many requests' },
    { status: 429, headers: { 'Retry-After': String(Math.ceil((ipLimit.resetAt.getTime() - Date.now()) / 1000)) } }
  );
}
```

After successful account creation (after the PDS createAccount call succeeds, before org initialization), record the attempt:
```ts
await recordRateLimitAttempt(`ip:${clientIp}`, 'onboard');
```

Only record on successful account creation (not on validation failures or PDS errors).

## Don't
- Change the FormData parsing, validation, invite verification, account creation, or org initialization logic
- Add email-based rate limiting (the invite code already gates account creation)
- Record attempts on validation failures

