## Files
- app/internal/analytics/interactive/components/cards/CardTimeMetrics.tsx (modify)

## What to do
The formatTime function (lines 10-14) receives seconds that may be fractional (e.g., 125.7). The current code does Math.floor(seconds / 60) for minutes but uses seconds %% 60 for secs, which preserves the fractional part (e.g., secs = 5.7).

Fix: normalize input to integer first.

Change:
```ts
const formatTime = (seconds: number): { minutes: number; secs: number } => {
    const minutes = Math.floor(seconds / 60);
    const secs = seconds %% 60;
    return { minutes, secs };
};
```
to:
```ts
const formatTime = (seconds: number): { minutes: number; secs: number } => {
    const total = Math.floor(seconds);
    const minutes = Math.floor(total / 60);
    const secs = total %% 60;
    return { minutes, secs };
};
```

## Don't
- Change the return type or interface
- Modify how the formatted values are displayed in the JSX
- Change animation timing

